  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ForumCiv EU-Belarus 2020-2023</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ForumCiv EU-Belarus 2020-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ForumCiv har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering av egeninsats om 3 820 388 SEK f&#xf6;r EU-projektet &quot;Build bridges, not walls: Reinvigorating Civil Society in Belarus&quot; f&#xf6;r perioden 2020-2023. 

Insatsen syftar till att: 

1. &quot;Empower local leaders and informal civic groups representing most marginalised groups (youth, women, people with disability etc.), activate grass&#x2014;root civic groups and their connections with their constituency&quot;.

2. &quot;Facilitate engagement of these groups with civil society experts based in Minsk which will bring collaboration between different layers of civil society to design and advocate for specific policy issues and praxis changes among duty&#x2014;bearers&quot;.

Forum Syd kommer att arbeta i samverkan med tre organisationer: Levania, Her Rights, och Youth Labour rights. Forum Syd &#xe4;r huvuds&#xf6;kande organisation och har det &#xf6;vergripande ansvaret f&#xf6;r projektets implementering och koordinering. 

Den aktuella insatsen har EU-kommissionens referensnummer EuropeAid/162112/DD/ACT/BY. Insatsen har en total budget p&#xe5; 1 296 917 EUR, vilket motsvarar cirka 13 920 445 SEK. Av detta har Forum Syd beviljats 947 900 EUR fr&#xe5;n EU-kommissionen och ans&#xf6;ker om 3 820 388 SEK (cirka 27%) fr&#xe5;n Sida.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ForumCiv has applied to Sida for funding of 3 820 388 SEK to carry out the &quot;Build bridges, not walls: Reinvigorating Civil Society in Belarus&quot; during the period 2020-2023. 

The project aims to: 

1. &quot;Empower local leaders and informal civic groups representing most marginalised groups (youth, women, people with disability etc.), activate grass&#x2014;root civic groups and their connections with their constituency&quot;.

2. &quot;Facilitate engagement of these groups with civil society experts based in Minsk which will bring collaboration between different layers of civil society to design and advocate for specific policy issues and praxis changes among duty&#x2014;bearers&quot;.

Forum Syd will collaborate with three civil society organizations: Levania, Her Rights, and Youth Labour rights. Forum Syd is lead applicant to Sida and has the overall responsibility for the coordination and implementation of the project. 

The contribution has the EU Commission reference number: EuropeAid/162112/DD/ACT/BY. The contribution&apos;s total budget is 1 296 917 EUR, which corresponds to approximately 13 920 445 SEK. The requested support from Sida is 3 820 388 SEK, which corresponds to 27% of the total budget.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsens &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att st&#xf6;dja &quot;Rigths holders&apos; in Belarus to have the capacity to affect decision-making processes and duty bearer practices through a reinvigorated and more representative Civil Society&quot;.

Insatsens specifika m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att &quot;empowering Belarusian Civil Society, represented by grassroots groups (GGS), CSOs and their networks to channel issues affecting rightsholders into decision making processes, will be achieved by carefully designed capacity development programmes, and by facilitating new and innovative cooperation platforms as well as targeted financial support to third parties&quot;.</narrative>
  </description>
